{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5451649/assistant-professor-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600096 Division Kinsley School of Engineering, Sciences, & Technology Department Electrical & Computer Engineering & Computer Science Opening Date 08/18/2026 Closing Date 11/15/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Electrical and Computer Engineering program at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering beginning in either January or August 2027, with ongoing in-person teaching assignments in the fall and spring terms each year. Our ABET-accredited Electrical and Computer Engineering program has roughly 100 undergraduate students, five full-time faculty, and three supporting staff members. Our hands-on program is known for small class sizes and extensive student/faculty interaction. Students participate in design/build/test projects throughout the curriculum, culminating in a year-long Capstone Design project. Nearly all of our instruction occurs in versatile state-of-the-art lecture/laboratory spaces. Our two-semester co-operative education requirement is a key component of our overall academic program, and is a substantive expression of our focus on pragmatic applications of concepts and skills embedded throughout our curriculum. Essential Functions For this position, we seek candidates that are eager to teach undergraduates in a student-centered, project-based learning environment. Applicants with a desire to utilize their knowledge and skills in mentoring undergraduates, conducting research with undergraduates, and teaching introductory electrical and computer engineering courses should apply. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate electrical and computer engineering related courses, including computer architecture, analog circuits, microprocessor and embedded systems, signal processing, and robotics. Other responsibilities may include advising students on independent study and capstone design projects, as well as teaching special topics in an area of expertise. The successful candidate will be active in curriculum and laboratory development and scholarly research. Experience and Education Required An earned Ph.D. in Computer or Electrical Engineering or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment is required. ABD will be considered. Required Skills and Qualifications Candidates are expected to demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching and advising, ongoing college service, professional development, developing undergraduate courses, and working with industry and undergraduate students in applied research. Further qualifications include the interest and ability to teach a wide range of undergraduate engineering courses. Top candidates will demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching and mentoring of undergraduates, and those candidates with teaching or industry experience are highly valued. Strong communication skills, the ability to work with undergraduate students, and ability to teach in a project-based setting are essential. Those candidates with research interests in embedded systems, robotics and autonomous systems, and machine learning or artificial intelligence are preferred. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you possess, or will you have by the start of the appointment, an earned Doctorate in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field? Yes No 02 Do you have interest in teaching a broad range of undergraduate engineering courses? Yes No 03 Do you have the ability to work effectively in a collegiate setting with students, faculty, administrators, and staff? Yes No 04 Do you have research interest in embedded systems, robotics, and autonomous systems, machine learning or artificial intelligence? Yes No 05 Do you have teaching experience? Yes No 06 Do you have industry experience? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5501600/assistant-professor-of-graphic-design": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600111 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department Department of the Visual and Performing Arts Opening Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date 11/16/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Department of Visual and Performing Arts at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Graphic Design in the Bachelor of Fine Arts (BFA) degree program beginning in August 2027. We seek an engaged educator and active practitioner with dedicated expertise in User Experience/User Interface Design and Motion Graphics. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in advancing our curriculum in interactive media, delivering high-impact studio instruction, and contributing to the academic and professional development of our undergraduate students. York College of Pennsylvania (YCP) thrives on cross-disciplinary collaboration, active creative practices, and faculty mentorship. We are a tight-knit community where your voice shapes the curriculum, your active studio practice is celebrated, and our gallery system and industry-standard studios provide a vibrant canvas for both you and YCP students. Located near major creative and cultural centers throughout the Mid-Atlantic region (Baltimore, New York City, Philadelphia, and Washington, D.C.), we are situated in a region with thriving creative entrepreneurship opportunities and community-engaged art. YCP can offer the perfect launchpad to connect your students with major cultural hubs while thriving in a supportive, collaborative peer environment. Additionally, the York art community provides opportunities for professional networking, internships, industry partnerships, and community engagement. York City's vibrant arts community further supports creative entrepreneurship, experiential learning, and partnerships that connect students with contemporary design practice. Outcome: The successful candidate will teach an engaging mix of foundational and advanced BFA courses, spanning from typography, identity systems, design research, and professional practice to UX/UI, and motion graphics with the opportunity to modernize and expand program offerings to reflect emerging trends in interactive media, emerging technologies, and contemporary design practice. Beyond cultivating student excellence in the studio environment, the successful candidate will provide dedicated mentorship through academic advising, engage in service to our academic community, and maintain a robust, active creative or scholarly practice supported by the institution. Essential Functions Teach four 3-credit courses per semester (Fall and Spring) Provide mentorship to students via academic advising Service to the college community Maintain an active scholarly and/or creative practice Experience and Education Required We are looking for a collaborative colleague who can bring a healthy mixture of classroom experience and real-world insight. Required: Terminal degree in Graphic Design, Interactive Media, Visual Communication, or a closely related field (MFA or equivalent). Demonstrated expertise in UX/UI Design and Motion Graphics software/workflows. Evidence of an active, high-level professional practice or scholarly record. A clear commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence and student mentorship with a minimum of two years of college-level teaching practice. Preferred: Minimum of three years of professional experience in the graphic design industry. Experience with cross-disciplinary collaboration or community-partnered design projects. Knowledge of emerging design technologies, including evolving AI-assisted workflows, accessibility standards, and creative entrepreneurship. Required Skills and Qualifications Additional Required Skills and Qualifications: Excellent communication skills and commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. Ability to supervise and motivate undergraduate students. To ensure full consideration, please submit the following materials electronically: 1. Cover letter detailing your teaching philosophy and professional practice 2. Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3. Link to digital portfolio of professional work 4. Link to portfolio of student work from courses taught 5. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts 6. Contact information for three confidential letters of recommendation Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have a Terminal Degree in Graphic Design or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5496059/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-biomedical-engineering": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Biomedical Engineering Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600107 Division Kinsley School of Engineering, Sciences, & Technology Department Civil & Mechanical Engineering Opening Date 09/25/2026 Closing Date 12/1/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary The Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering program at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a tenure-track (open rank) Professor of Biomedical Engineering position beginning in the Fall 2027 semester, coinciding with the arrival of the first class of students for our new Biomedical Engineering program. The overall department houses approximately 300 undergraduates, eleven full-time faculty members, and five part-time and full-time staff members. The ABET-accredited programs in our department are characterized as hands-on with small class sizes and extensive student/faculty interactions. Students in the engineering departments participate in design/build/test projects throughout the curriculum, culminating with a yearlong Capstone Design project that requires a functioning prototype. This includes several courses in our state-of-the-art Materials Science and Fluid Mechanics laboratories. A keystone of the York College engineering programs is that our students participate in two semesters of engineering work in an industry setting as part of our required co-operative learning program prior to graduation. This gives our students valuable experience that they can then apply in their classroom learning. For this position, we seek candidates that are eager to teach undergraduates in a student-centered, project-based learning environment. Applicants with a desire to utilize their knowledge and skills in mentoring undergraduates, conducting research with undergraduates, and teaching introductory engineering courses should apply. Expertise across all areas of biomedical engineering is valued, however, knowledge of quantitative physiology and bioinstrumentation are especially valued. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate foundational and biomedical engineering courses throughout the fall and spring semesters. Additionally, the successful candidate will be expected to advise undergraduate students regarding their course curriculum and on career matters; perform service to the department, college, and/or community; and show the potential for research work that can involve undergraduate students. The successful candidate will also help develop and refine the courses within the new Biomedical Engineering program. Experience and Education Required Applicants must have an Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. Required Skills and Qualifications Further qualifications include the interest and ability to teach undergraduate engineering courses in the area of bioinstrumentation and quantitative physiology. Top candidates will demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching, and those candidates with prior teaching experience are highly valued. Strong communication skills, the ability to work with undergraduate students, and ability to teach in a project-based setting are essential. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have an earned Doctorate in Biomedical Engineering or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No 03 Do you have non-academic work experience related to biomedical engineering, mechanical engineering, or a related field? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5364759/adjunct-clinical-faculty-for-undergraduate-nursing": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Faculty for Undergraduate Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical Faculty for Undergraduate Nursing Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Part Time Job Number 202600056 Division School of Nursing & Health Professionals Department Nursing Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date 11/30/2026 9:30 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Stabler Department of Nursing is seeking to hire qualified adjunct clinical faculty with experience in medical-surgical or women’s health nursing to provide clinical instruction in the Baccalaureate degree program. Adjunct faculty are expected to instruct students in the clinical setting; provide support and guidance; and evaluate performance of learning outcomes. Outcome: Successful hiring of at least 4 adjunct faculty to teach an undergraduate nursing clinical for NUR334/335 or NUR328/329 Essential Functions Maintains current knowledge related to clinical policies and procedures. Keeps the course coordinator informed of all student and agency issues and concerns. Serves as a professional role model for other faculty, staff, and students in the clinical setting. Evaluates weekly assignments and provides feedback to students in a timely manner. Adheres to applicable regulatory rules and standards. Experience and Education Required Licensure as a Registered Nurse in Pennsylvania Baccalaureate degree in nursing Graduate degree in nursing or plans to complete a graduate degree within 5 years Expertise and experience in medical-surgical or women’s health nursing Required Skills and Qualifications Candidates must demonstrate excellent communication skills and have a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team. Adjunct faculty work in collaboration with full-time faculty to provide a safe and supportive learning environment that assists students in the integration of knowledge, interprofessional communication, and development of professional values in the clinical practice setting. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . Part-time employees are eligible to make elective retirement contributions on a pretax basis as described in the college's Retirement Benefit Plan. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have the ability to work effectively in a collegiate setting with students, faculty, administrators, and staff? Yes No 02 Do you have a valid RN License in Pennsylvania? Yes No 03 Do you have a Bachelor's Degree in Nursing? Yes No 04 Do you have a Master's Degree in Nursing or plans to complete one within 5 years? Yes No 05 Do you have at least one year of experience in medical-surgical or women's health nursing? Yes No 06 Do you have the ability to function capably in a fast-paced work environment? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5532543/adjunct-instructor-of-art-sculpture": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Art - Sculpture",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Art - Sculpture Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Part Time Job Number 202600122 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department Department of the Visual and Performing Arts Opening Date 10/28/2026 Closing Date 12/10/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for an adjunct instructor in Sculpture for Spring 2027 to teach Sculpture, working with beginning through advanced students within the same class sessions. The course serves Fine Art majors and students in the general education program. Responsibilities include course preparation, instruction, assessment, student support, office hours, and communication with department faculty and administration. Outcome: The successful candidate will teach Sculpture, working with beginning through advanced students within the same class sessions. The course schedule is Mondays and Wednesdays, 2:00-4:30 in person. Essential Functions Course Development and Delivery Develop, deliver, and maintain syllabi and course materials for four levels of Sculpture. Instruction should address a variety of sculptural techniques, historical art movements, and professional practices appropriate to each course level. Create a classroom environment that encourages active learning, experimentation, and individual artistic development. Maintain course materials, assignments, grades, and schedules through Canvas. Student Engagement Foster an inclusive and supportive studio environment that accommodates students with different levels of experience. Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and projects, along with individual guidance when needed. Assessment and Evaluation Develop and administer assessments consistent with departmental guidelines. Evaluate student work based on course objectives, technical development, creative problem-solving, and artistic growth. Additional Responsibilities Maintain familiarity with college and studio facilities policies and procedures. Communicate student concerns and course-related issues to the department as appropriate. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and administration to support student success. Maintain professional standards in communication, attendance, and instructional responsibilities. Experience and Education Required A bachelor's degree in Fine Arts or a related field is required. An MFA in Sculpture, Fine Arts, or a related field is preferred. 1-3 years of college-level teaching experience is strongly preferred, including teaching experience gained during graduate study. Professional experience in sculpture is desirable. Required Skills and Qualifications Required Skills and Qualifications: Strong interpersonal, observational, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and with varying levels of artistic experience. Demonstrated patience, adaptability, and commitment to student development. Preferred A record of published work or other professional contributions to the field of sculpture. Participation in professional conferences, exhibitions, or workshops. Experience integrating technology into teaching. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . Part-time employees are eligible to make elective retirement contributions on a pretax basis as described in the college's Retirement Benefit Plan. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have at least three years of professional experience as a sculptor? Yes No 02 Do you have a Bachelor's degree in a related field? Yes No 03 Do you have a Master's degree in a related field? Yes No 04 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5524174/adjunct-instructor-creative-writing": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Creative Writing",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Creative Writing Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Part Time Job Number 202600116 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department Communication and Writing Opening Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date 12/1/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Adjunct Instructor in Creative Writing will be responsible for teaching CRW 272: Introduction to Creative Writing. They will meet regularly with the class and teach a broad range of creative writing craft, including fiction, poetry, and creative nonfiction. The instructor will use Canvas to post course materials, grade assignments, and communicate with students throughout the course. Instructors are required to host office hours for in-person advising meetings with students. The instructor will be expected to engage in meetings and faculty development outside the classroom as needed and participate in any program assessment as required. Essential Functions Prepares for and teaches all assigned courses as scheduled Holds office hours as required Evaluates and provides feedback to students in a timely manner Uses the college’s course learning management software to post materials, assignments, and course grades Follows all college-wide and department policies Participates in faculty development meetings as necessary Participates in regular outcomes assessment work Experience and Education Required The candidate should possess an advanced degree in creative writing (or related field), such as an MA, MFA, or PhD, or a publication record that would be equivalent to such experience. Candidates with recent or forthcoming literary publications in peer-reviewed venues are preferable. Ideally, the candidate should have experience in the undergraduate college classroom. Required Skills and Qualifications The candidate should demonstrate excellent communication skills and have a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team. Please submit electronically in addition to cover letter, resume and 3 references, the following: Graduate transcripts Teaching evaluations A letter of application Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . Part-time employees are eligible to make elective retirement contributions on a pretax basis as described in the college's Retirement Benefit Plan. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have a Master or Doctorate Degree in Creative Writing or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No 03 Do you have the ability to work effectively in a collegiate setting with students, faculty, administrators, and staff? Yes No 04 Have you had work published in a peer-reviewed journal in the field of creative writing? Yes No 05 Have you presented your creative writing research or literary work at a conference or professional literary event? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5526908/assistant-associate-professor-of-film-and-media-arts-open-rank-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Film and Media Arts (Open Rank & Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Film and Media Arts (Open Rank & Tenure-Track) Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600117 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department Department of the Visual and Performing Arts Opening Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date 12/15/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Department of Communication and Writing seeks an imaginative, forward-thinking educator and filmmaker with experience in teaching narrative film production to join a growing, engaged, student-centered Department of Communication and Writing. Our nine faculty members and dedicated adjunct faculty, who represent programs in Film and Media Arts, Mass Communication, and English and Writing, share a passion for teaching and mentoring undergraduate students, embracing new technologies, and preparing graduates who are sought after by regional and national employers. The successful candidate will join the Film and Media Arts program, where collaboration is deeply embedded in the culture. With outstanding production facilities, including a professional-grade studio, dedicated editing bays, and an extensive equipment inventory, the department provides the tools and institutional support faculty and students need to produce award-winning work. Teaching four courses per semester, the successful candidate will help students take original narrative film projects from concept to completion in collaboration with one another while building the technical and professional skills required by the film industry and other industries focused on the creation and analysis of media content. Through a campus-wide culture of colleagues who are eager to work across disciplinary boundaries, the program maintains strong partnerships with Mass Communication and Sport Media, and the successful candidate will join colleagues in building new opportunities, integrating emerging technologies, and contributing to a vibrant culture of learning and success. A hallmark of a York College education is our commitment to engage students in real-world experiences. Our faculty are encouraged to develop coursework and partnerships with nonprofits and industry partners, where students work hand-in-hand with practitioners to create materials and solutions that serve our community. Students in the department consistently win and place in the Broadcast Education Association Festival of Media Arts and On Location Competitions, as well as the College Broadcasters Inc. Awards. In addition to these national awards, our students showcase their work at the Film and Media Arts annual Student Film event and participate in clubs such as the Film and Media Society and WVYC 88.1 FM: The York College Radio Station. Our graduates go on to successful careers across the film and media spectrum, from local news outlets and media companies to national outlets such as ESPN and Netflix. Facilities & Resources Our programs are backed by outstanding production facilities and a supportive institutional ecosystem that helps students produce exceptional work: Film Viewing Room: A purpose-built film theater with high-definition digital projection and a 7.1 surround sound system. Purpose-Built Production Studios: A professional-grade studio complex including a TV studio, a dedicated control room, studio space for set construction, a green screen, and industry-standard equipment. Editing Bays & Post-Production Facilities: Three dedicated editing bays with fast-processing computers and additional editing and production spaces to support coursework, student projects, and faculty creative work. High-Quality Equipment: A strong, growing inventory of cameras, audio gear, lighting, and accessories available for both student and faculty use. Outcome: The successful candidate will strengthen the Film and Media Arts curriculum, guiding students as they develop original narrative work and preparing them for careers in film and media, while remaining professionally active. Essential Functions Teach introductory through advanced production courses, with an emphasis on narrative filmmaking. Advise and mentor students, including academic advising, independent studies, internship support, and preparation for careers or graduate study. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Maintain an active professional and scholarly agenda. Experience and Education Required MFA (or equivalent terminal degree) in film production, directing, screenwriting, cinematography, or a closely related field, completed by August 2027. Demonstrated effectiveness teaching undergraduate production courses, including experience as instructor of record. Demonstrated experience producing narrative films, with a strong grasp of cinematic storytelling and film set culture and crew roles. Required Skills and Qualifications Excellent college-level teaching skills and the ability to utilize educational technology to support student learning and success. Student-focused approach, with the ability to learn and apply new concepts and ideas to support our diverse population of learners. Excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team. Ability to apply supervisory skills and motivate undergraduate students. Experience with the tools and techniques necessary to write, shoot, edit, and mix narrative films. Project management experience and the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Ability to lift at least 50 lbs. Applicants should submit a Teaching Statement, a link to a reel of their narrative film work, and information for three confidential letters of recommendation. Finalists will be asked to provide two sample syllabi for undergraduate courses they have designed and taught as the instructor of record related to the position. At least one sample syllabus should be from an introductory or lower-level production-related course. Finalists will be expected to demonstrate competence with filmmaking tools and techniques as part of the on-campus interview process. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you possess a MFA (or equivalent terminal degree) in film production, directing, screenwriting, cinematography, or a closely related field, completed by August 2027? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching undergraduate production courses as instructor of record? Yes No 03 Do you have experience in film production as a director, producer, or other high-level crew member? Yes No 04 Do you have experience in the creation of narrative films, especially short films? Yes No 05 Do you have the ability to work effectively in a collegiate setting with students, faculty, administrators, and staff? Yes No 06 Do you have the ability to function capably in a fast-paced work environment? Yes No 07 Are you able to lift at least 50 lbs.? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5532403/master-of-public-policy-administration-program-dir-tenure-track-professor-of-p": {
      "title": "Master of Public Policy & Administration Program Dir./Tenure-Track Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Master of Public Policy & Administration Program Dir./Tenure-Track Professor of Political Science Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600121 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department History & Political Science Opening Date 10/28/2026 Closing Date 11/30/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary The Office of Graduate and Professional Programs and the Department of History and Political Science at York College of Pennsylvania (YCP) invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position in political science who will serve as the Director for the Master of Public Policy and Administration (MPPA) graduate program beginning in Summer 2027. The MPPA graduate program is established with approximately 25 graduate students enrolled. The successful candidate will help shape the future of civic engagement and graduate education at York College of Pennsylvania as the leader who will guide our MPPA graduate program for years to come. The candidate will embark on an exciting opportunity to establish a vision for the future of this masters program and promote it to the Central Pennsylvania policy and governance community and beyond. They will also be able to immediately connect with our local community through previously established partnerships and have opportunities to further extend these community connections and engagement as they work to build new partnerships and respond to community needs. Additionally, they will have the opportunity to shape the knowledge, skills, and mindsets that will equip our dedicated working professional masters and doctoral students in the next phase of their professional careers. As the MPPA Graduate Director, the successful candidate will work closely with the Director of Graduate and Professional Programs to support students from the very beginning of their graduate career through the review of applications, orientation of new students, advising throughout their program, and participating in graduation events. This position offers the unique opportunity to lead a graduate program and connect with graduate students from ‘app to cap’! The successful candidate will contribute their expertise in public policy and American government to our vibrant undergraduate program in political science. In keeping with YCP’s signature focus on hands-on learning, there are opportunities to collaborate with the Arthur J. Glatfelter Institute for Public Policy to connect classroom theory with actionable community solutions through nonpartisan research, public events, and civic partnerships for both graduate and undergraduate students. YCP is located near the state capital in Harrisburg and within reach of Baltimore, Philadelphia, and Washington, D.C., giving faculty and students ready access to government at the local, state, and federal levels. Essential Functions Teach five 3-credit courses, at least three at the graduate level, across fall, spring, and summer (2/2/1 teaching load) Maintain an active scholarly agenda consistent with college and disciplinary standards Lead graduate recruitment initiatives by nurturing and expanding community partnerships Admit, orient, and advise students in the MPPA Program Manage graduate class scheduling and coordination of instructors Participate in graduate initiatives led by the Director of Graduate and Professional Programs Engage in additional service to the college, as needed Experience and Education Required Ph.D. in Political Science or a closely related field by the start of the appointment Minimum of 1 year of administrative experience, preferably directing one or more programs Ability to offer upper-level courses in Public Policy and/or State and Local Government. Ability to offer introductory-level courses, such as American Government and/or Introduction to Political Science Minimum 2 years of experience teaching in higher education Minimum of 1 year of experience teaching at the masters level Minimum of 1 year of experience teaching in a variety of modalities (in-person, hybrid, online) Required Skills and Qualifications The candidate must demonstrate excellent communication skills and have a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team. Qualifications include the ability to communicate with students and the public, apply supervisory skills, motivate students, be personable and professional, have patience with and understanding of students, and be able to learn and apply new concepts and ideas. Additionally, the candidate must have the ability to offer upper-level courses in Public Policy and/or State and Local Government and introductory-level courses, such as American Government and/or Introduction to Political Science. Candidates invited to online interviews will be asked to submit a Teaching Statement and example Teaching Evaluations. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you possess an earned Doctorate in Political Science or a closely related field or expect to by July 2027? Yes No 02 Do you have at least 2 years of experience teaching in Higher education? Yes No 03 Do you have at least 1 year of administrative experience? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5528113/tenure-track-professor-of-political-science-open-rank": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Professor of Political Science (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Professor of Political Science (Open Rank) Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600119 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department History & Political Science Opening Date 10/26/2026 Closing Date 11/25/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary The Department of History and Political Science at York College of Pennsylvania (YCP) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position beginning in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will join a student-centered department. This department consists of 16 FT faculty members who, along with excellent adjunct faculty, teach in several majors including History, Political Science, Intelligence Analysis, Philosophy, and International Relations. All of these faculty are passionate about teaching and mentoring undergraduate students, and preparing graduates for regional and national employment opportunities. This appointment can be made at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor depending on qualifications. The successful candidate will help shape the future of civic engagement and pre-law education at York College of Pennsylvania as a driving force behind our American politics curriculum. In this role, you will teach and mentor motivated undergraduates, while serving as a champion for our expanding Political Science & Law 3+3 program—an accelerated pathway enabling students to earn both a BA and JD in six years. You will engage our students in challenging coursework, prepare our students for successful careers, and empower the next generation of policy, legal, and public service leaders. In keeping with YCP’s signature focus on hands-on learning, you would be able to collaborate with the Arthur J. Glatfelter Institute for Public Policy and other campus entities, creating opportunities to connect classroom theory with actionable community solutions through nonpartisan research, public events, and civic partnerships. The position carries a 4/4 teaching load, you will engage students at every stage of their academic journey—inspiring non-majors in general education courses like American Government and Introduction to Political Science, while delivering specialized upper-level seminars in American political institutions, American law, state and local government, and statistical methods. YCP is located near the state capital in Harrisburg and within easy reach of Baltimore, Philadelphia, and Washington, D.C., giving faculty and students ready access to government at the local, state, and federal levels. Essential Functions Teach four 3-credit courses per semester (4/4 teaching load) Advise students in the Political Science and Political Science & Law 3+3 majors Maintain an active scholarly agenda consistent with college and disciplinary standards Service to the college Experience and Education Required Ph.D. in Political Science or a closely related field; ABD candidates near completion will be considered. Ability to offer upper-level courses in American political institutions and/or American law, state and local government, and statistical methods in political science. Ability to offer introductory-level courses, such as American Government and/or Introduction to Political Science At least 1 year experience teaching in higher education. Required Skills and Qualifications Application Instructions To ensure full consideration, please submit the following materials electronically: Cover letter articulating your teaching experience and research agenda Curriculum Vitae (CV) Unofficial graduate transcripts Contact information for three references Candidates invited to online interviews will be asked to submit a Teaching Statement. The review of applications will begin immediately. Questions should be submitted to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Nick Anspach (NAnspach@ycp.edu). Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you possess a doctorate with a focus in political science (or a closely related field), or expect to by August 2027? Yes No 02 Do you have two or more semesters of experience teaching in higher education? Yes No 03 Do you have two or more semesters of experience teaching or working in the field of American institutions and/or American Law? Yes No 04 Have you presented your research or scholarly work at a national association conference? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"
    }
  },
